    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1081">

                <pb facs="0806" n="730" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg730"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.512/1363</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Special Representative Rodgers to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-08-24T16:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 24 1916, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>314. Department’s 316 August 23, 7 p.m. Cabrera informed me definitely this
                    morning that there would be no extension time payment without penalty mining
                    taxes for last tercio, this decision which he considered final being for reasons
                    communicated to me yesterday and incorporated in my 208. Have no reason to
                    believe there will be alteration this program at present.</p>
                <p>Two months grace with penalty twenty-five per cent September and perhaps fifty
                    per cent October will be granted according to present plan.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rodgers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
